{
    "word": "choleric",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f2d8e3f9-ad49-38d9-aba9-725a18093de0",
                "word": "choleric",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d3735f86-2e2e-410c-a904-ae6630f7cdc1",
                        "entry_id": "f2d8e3f9-ad49-38d9-aba9-725a18093de0",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more choleric"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "ce3d1ac5-4db5-44ea-86a6-3e885b583edf",
                        "entry_id": "f2d8e3f9-ad49-38d9-aba9-725a18093de0",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most choleric"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "94118b5e-d875-371f-972c-fb29ce56cf0e",
                        "entry_id": "f2d8e3f9-ad49-38d9-aba9-725a18093de0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a temperament characterized by an excess of choler; easily becoming angry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c02579c-13f2-4bda-88e6-ecda2b056b31",
                                "sense_id": "94118b5e-d875-371f-972c-fb29ce56cf0e",
                                "text": "And let a man beware, how he keepeth company with choleric and quarrelsome persons; for they will engage him into their own quarrels."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d424203b-cee9-452d-997e-40a12e1dc5e5",
                                "sense_id": "94118b5e-d875-371f-972c-fb29ce56cf0e",
                                "text": "1640, George Herbert, Jacula Prudentum; or, Outlandish Proverbs, Sentences, etc., in The Remains of that Sweet Singer of the Temple George Herbert, London: Pickering, 1841, p. 146,\nFrom a choleric man withdraw a little; from him that says nothing for ever."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "67f6d0ac-acab-4ec8-925b-24825573dda8",
                                "sense_id": "94118b5e-d875-371f-972c-fb29ce56cf0e",
                                "text": "As it was clear that he was a choleric fellow in some respects, Mr Swiveller was relieved to find him in such good humour, and, to encourage him in it, smiled himself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e82ec119-ec04-491a-af3e-4ecabe4a1003",
                                "sense_id": "94118b5e-d875-371f-972c-fb29ce56cf0e",
                                "text": "Beneath his choleric exterior Gerald O’Hara had the tenderest of hearts."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cebb25eb-2361-3ced-8392-8734b9a885e6",
                        "entry_id": "f2d8e3f9-ad49-38d9-aba9-725a18093de0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Showing or expressing anger."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3dd8ab30-9078-4dcc-942a-3dde90c07ce8",
                                "sense_id": "cebb25eb-2361-3ced-8392-8734b9a885e6",
                                "text": "What, what, my lord! are you so choleric\nWith Eleanor, for telling but her dream?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7cff0a1a-c5b3-4944-bae4-bb9a352326e2",
                                "sense_id": "cebb25eb-2361-3ced-8392-8734b9a885e6",
                                "text": "How angry the poor devil is! In fine, thou art as choleric as a cook by a fireside."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2c730ef-0f6c-4890-9c0a-0623399175e9",
                                "sense_id": "cebb25eb-2361-3ced-8392-8734b9a885e6",
                                "text": "For God’s ſake, Madam, vvhy ſo Cholerick? I ſay, this Letter is ſome Forgery; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b8745db-af53-447b-9783-183dae464083",
                                "sense_id": "cebb25eb-2361-3ced-8392-8734b9a885e6",
                                "text": "[As] in most revolutionary movements, counterrevolutionary action was dealt with harshly – witness Lucas's (1994) choleric reaction to Ball and Mankiw (1994)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0c15f449-7029-31a8-adf5-3a8243e13550",
                        "entry_id": "f2d8e3f9-ad49-38d9-aba9-725a18093de0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to cholera (infectious disease)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "03c44bbe-df07-4226-95af-bb08a772b613",
                                "sense_id": "0c15f449-7029-31a8-adf5-3a8243e13550",
                                "text": "I now proceed to enumerate those lesions and morbid changes found in the bodies of those cut off by cholera, which must have preceded the appearance of the disease, and which, existing, as they did, in very different organs, had no connection with the choleric symptoms, but nevertheless rendered the chance of recovery much less likely."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c11c380f-9e3c-34bf-8ccd-48fbfae4a8a2",
                        "entry_id": "f2d8e3f9-ad49-38d9-aba9-725a18093de0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Causing an excess of choler."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0df87bac-0063-4524-8cee-6de5e3d329cd",
                                "sense_id": "c11c380f-9e3c-34bf-8ccd-48fbfae4a8a2",
                                "text": "I fear it is too choleric a meat.\nHow say you to a fat tripe finely broil’d?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36f865b9-cc15-431c-8881-81a32be96df1",
